WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.000
The year was 1991. It was a quiet&nbsp;
night in Lethargy Valley, Arizona,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.560
the quietest town in all of Maricopa County.&nbsp;
Seriously, despite the hardcore Arizona dry heat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:17.680
this is one of the most idyllic little towns&nbsp;
you could imagine. Everyone who lived there knew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:23.200
each other by name and regularly invited their&nbsp;
neighbors to wholesome neighborhood cookouts. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.720
town’s historic main street had an old-fashioned&nbsp;
ice cream parlor, a knitting supplies store,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:36.000
and even a Build-A-Bear workshop. And of course,&nbsp;
a few local car dealerships and auto body shops.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.280
Lethargy Valley really is just the sweetest,&nbsp;
calmest place you can possibly imagine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.680
and tonight, my friends, it’s going to rock.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.600
While the citizens of Lethargy Valley&nbsp;
went about their evening duties,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:57.040
something hardcore was heading their way, rumbling&nbsp;
across the scorching Arizona deserts, burning fuel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:04.320
and belching smog. The hottest hot rods this side&nbsp;
of the sun. Wheels so fly they’re ready to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:11.520
off, with riders so badass their own reflections&nbsp;
are scared of them. That’s right: These are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:17.440
the High-Octane Full-Throttle Adventures of the&nbsp;
Exploding Zombie Gearheads, and they’re about to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:24.080
give this sleepy Arizona town a Four-Loko enema.
The sun was setting on Lethargy Valley when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:29.840
lights of distant fire cut through the night.&nbsp;
Citizens and shopkeepers, enjoying an evening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:36.000
summer breeze, halted in town as the redness in&nbsp;
the East got closer and brighter. They could feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.280
the rumble of torqued-up subwoofers rattling&nbsp;
the ground. The roar of the engines felt more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:47.600
fitting on 747s than road-legal cars. And when&nbsp;
the distance was close enough that they could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:53.760
taste the vapors of burning gasoline in the&nbsp;
air, they could finally hear the laughter, too.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:02:00.880
Meet SCP-3885-01, also known as&nbsp;
the Exploding Zombie Gearheads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:06.320
probably the most metal of all anomalies on&nbsp;
the SCP Foundation catalog. But let’s talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.880
about the time before these gas-chugging dust&nbsp;
devils were just another number in The Man’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:17.920
filing cabinet. Cause these bad boys don’t care&nbsp;
about filing - They only care about defiling.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:22.560
They rolled into Lethargy Valley like a&nbsp;
pack of easy-riding coyotes on gearhead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:29.520
steroids. Their skin is green from rot, and&nbsp;
covered in cuts, lesions, and gnarly burn scars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:35.200
Some have their heads completely cracked open,&nbsp;
exposing what little brains they have underneath.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:40.240
Others have fully opened rib cages and&nbsp;
disemboweled bellies. But they don’t care.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:46.880
These ain’t your grandpa’s zombies. Forget the&nbsp;
Walking Dead, these dudes are the Riding Dead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:52.000
Romero meets Ratfink after ten lines of&nbsp;
Columbian Bam-Bam and a gallon of Monster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:57.920
Energy drink, decked out in a patchwork of&nbsp;
Motorhead-style leather and stolen clothes.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:03.440
And you better believe these fun-dead&nbsp;
freakazoids are here to party hardy.&nbsp;

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:09.200
Paulie Poundtown rounded the corner of Main street&nbsp;
first on his ride, The Murderlizer. In a past&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:14.080
life, it’d been a coffin, but now, with the aid of&nbsp;
two monster truck wheels on the back and a pair of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:20.480
circular saw blades on the front, it was a vehicle&nbsp;
ready to tear up the streets. Literally. Paulie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:26.160
drove down the road at a break-neck pace, leaving&nbsp;
a trail of sparks and black smog behind him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:31.600
He was screaming something about being king of the&nbsp;
world when the vehicle exploded underneath him.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:35.920
The force of the boom flung Paulie down the&nbsp;
length of the street. He hit the window of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:41.680
local barbershop and shattered through it like a&nbsp;
fleshy missile. For a moment, he lay on the tiles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:46.240
a leather pincushion of broken glass and&nbsp;
wooden shrapnel from the recently-detonated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:51.360
Murderlizer. But at no moment in this&nbsp;
whole insane ordeal did Paulie stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:56.320
laughing. He got up, noticing his neck was&nbsp;
twisted backward at an odd angle - we told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.320 --> 00:04:00.800
you it was a break-neck pace - but Paulie&nbsp;
just grabbed that sucker and crunched it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:06.480
back into place. It’d take a little more than&nbsp;
a totaled spine to stop Paulie Poundtown.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.800
After all, the night’s fun was only just starting.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.800
More tricked-out zombie roadsters were&nbsp;
pouring into the town from every angle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:19.680
hopped up on a combination of tequila, lighter&nbsp;
fluid, and some stuff we can’t even mention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:25.040
if we want to keep monetization on this video.&nbsp;
Steely Dan was roaring into the Build-A-Bear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:30.240
workshop on a modified toilet with all-crushing&nbsp;
caterpillar tracks. Once he’d busted in through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:34.960
the facade, he dismounted his porcelain throne&nbsp;
and began incinerating walls of teddy bears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:39.840
with a custom flamethrower powered by&nbsp;
a tube going into his stomach cavity.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:44.480
Once he was done burning 90% of the bears in&nbsp;
the store, he used the remaining unsullied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:49.120
parts to make a grungy-looking bear in his&nbsp;
own likeness. He strapped it to the front&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:54.480
of his terrifying mobile toilet, and then&nbsp;
burnt that, too, just for the fun of it.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:59.040
Bareback Boris was making a beeline for the&nbsp;
ice cream parlor, riding what would look like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:04.480
a bull to the untrained eye. It was actually&nbsp;
a taxidermied bull, gutted and filled with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:08.960
nightmarish configuration of motorcycle parts&nbsp;
that would function better together as a method&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:15.440
of execution than a workable vehicle, but that’s&nbsp;
just how the Exploding Zombie Gearheads like it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:18.720
Boris pulled the handbrake, which&nbsp;
was made out of some old bones he dug&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:23.200
up once, and ground the Bullcycle to a&nbsp;
screeching halt in front of the parlor.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:27.600
He climbed off and kicked in the door,&nbsp;
before running in to cause some chaos.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:33.520
Boris, the animal that he was, grabbed handfuls&nbsp;
of gelato and shoved them into his mouth, before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:39.120
turning and spitting them at the wall. He pulled&nbsp;
out a bottle of 90% vodka and took a long swig,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:43.520
before taking a court summons out of his&nbsp;
jacket and shoving it into the bottle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:47.920
He lit the top of the litigious fuse with&nbsp;
his lighter, which was shaped like a knife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:53.680
and made a molotov cocktail. Moments&nbsp;
later, the whole store was in flames.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.720
Boris stepped out of the burning ice cream&nbsp;
parlor, on fire but utterly unphased. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:03.040
pulled out no less than four cigars&nbsp;
and lit them on his own burning skin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:07.600
before smoking each one in a single&nbsp;
pull. If his lungs didn’t already look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:12.160
like blackened lumps of decaying coal,&nbsp;
they would have been screaming at him.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:16.640
But right now, the only person screaming&nbsp;
was Gene Simmons of the band KISS,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:22.080
as some of Boris’ fellow riders rampaged through&nbsp;
the streets past him, “UNHOLY” blaring from their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:27.840
radios at ear-exploding volumes. The Exploding&nbsp;
Zombie Gearheads didn’t throw out-of-town ragers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:33.600
like this often, but when they did, they always&nbsp;
tried to make it one for the history books. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:38.800
before you start worrying about the safety of the&nbsp;
citizens of Lethargy Valley, Arizona, you should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:45.360
know that the Zombie Gearheads never hurt anybody.&nbsp;
Well, never hurt anybody on purpose, that is.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:50.720
If a piece of stray shrapnel from an exploding&nbsp;
Camaro, reshaped with scrap metal to look like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:56.640
a giant fist spraying fire from its knuckles,&nbsp;
happens to take out somebody’s eye, well...That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:03.040
can’t really be seen as anybody’s fault, can&nbsp;
it? Especially when you don’t have eyes anymore.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:08.320
The closest thing to the brains of this operation&nbsp;
- which, for these guys, really isn’t saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:13.200
much - was a free-thinking, free-spirited,&nbsp;
free-liquored individual known as Joey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:18.480
nuts. The whole gang had probably&nbsp;
about 40 brain cells between them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:23.120
but at least five of those cells belonged to&nbsp;
Joey. While many of his rotting buddies were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:28.400
goofing off and causing mayhem across town,&nbsp;
Joey was already acting on the real reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:33.840
everybody was here: Getting new parts&nbsp;
for their sick-as-all-hell car mods.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:38.400
Sure, as mechanics, they couldn’t produce&nbsp;
actually workable vehicles worth a damn.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:42.240
But at the end of the day, isn’t a vehicle&nbsp;
looking awesome much more important than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:47.120
boring old functionality? If you think&nbsp;
otherwise, you’re probably just a square.

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:54.880
But we digress, back to Joey nuts. Joey and&nbsp;
a crew of his boys - including Dirty Mike,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.880 --> 00:08:00.320
Scuzzy Steve, and Generally Unclean Gary - rolled&nbsp;
up on one of the local auto body shops and bashed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:05.440
the door down with their vehicle. Which,&nbsp;
by the way, was a modified SUV modded with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:11.680
bulldozer parts and a makeshift cannon. It was&nbsp;
a powerful, if structurally unsound, motorized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:16.000
siege weapon. Joey and the boys jumped off&nbsp;
the vehicle and stormed into the building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.760
wielding pipe wrenches with nails&nbsp;
and fishing hooks welded onto them.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:24.720
A confused mechanic was quaking in his boots as&nbsp;
the gaggle of zombie gearheads approached him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:28.960
Joey stood at the front, swinging his pipe&nbsp;
wrench around with menacing randomness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:33.360
He was chewing twelve toothpicks,&nbsp;
making him look extra tough.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.920
The mechanic, with a quiet, trembling voice,&nbsp;
told Joey and the boys that they needed to leave.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:41.760
They weren’t supposed to be back here.&nbsp;
They’d need to leave and come back during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:46.560
opening hours. It was the most polite&nbsp;
telling-off he could possibly muster.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:50.800
The exploding zombie gearheads just&nbsp;
laughed. Once they were done cackling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:56.240
Joey lifted up his pipe wrench and pointed it&nbsp;
at the terrified mechanic’s face. Joey cleared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:59.280
his tobacco-and-gasoline-burned throat and said:

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:03.920
“Listen, ya stupid grease monkey, I’m only&nbsp;
gonna say this once so open your earholes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:08.880
real wide and listen up, ‘kay? You’re gonna&nbsp;
pack up your crap and leave, so me and my boys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:14.640
can loot this place to our heart’s content, and&nbsp;
beef up our sick-ass rides. And if you don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:21.600
leave? You’re gonna be holding this here pipe&nbsp;
wrench for me in your prison pocket. You get me?”

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:26.720
The mechanic definitely got him. He didn’t&nbsp;
waste a moment in high-tailing it out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:31.280
the store while Joey and the boys pulled&nbsp;
a classic “smash and grab” on his wares.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:36.240
They stole everything from whole cars&nbsp;
to wrenches and lug nuts. Across town,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:41.520
the Exploding Zombie Gearheads were doing the&nbsp;
exact same thing: Stealing or stripping every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:47.120
vehicle in sight and cannibalizing the parts&nbsp;
for their own righteous whips. Town by town,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:54.560
vehicle by vehicle, explosion by explosion, they’d&nbsp;
one day figure this whole “mechanic” deal out.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:59.520
With the night’s revelry finally concluded, it was&nbsp;
time to return home and get to work on the next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:05.440
set of rides. This legion of awesome, unkillable&nbsp;
morons piled back into their stylish death traps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:10.560
and rode off into the misty dawn, leaving&nbsp;
hundreds of thousands of dollars in property&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:16.320
damage behind them - But not a single&nbsp;
death. As hyper-destructive anomalies go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:21.760
they’re honestly pretty benevolent. Or at&nbsp;
least, too self-centered to be truly malevolent.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:28.080
They tore up the desert on the way back&nbsp;
to the real SCP-3885: Vulture Gulch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:33.600
the home of the Exploding Zombie Gearheads.&nbsp;
It’s a desert shantytown that’s “officially”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:40.160
been abandoned since July 9th, 1973, due to high&nbsp;
volumes of dangerous radon gas being emitted from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:45.920
the uranium deposits in a nearby mine. But these&nbsp;
intense, joy-riding mutants hardly mind a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:53.920
bit of radiation in their sweet pad. Be it ever&nbsp;
so radioactive, there’s no place like home, right?

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:57.200
Some of the vehicles even exploded&nbsp;
on the way back to the place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.200 --> 00:11:02.880
but the boys didn’t mind. The flaming explosion&nbsp;
survivors just crawled out of the fire and hopped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:08.240
onto the rides of their closest buddies. All&nbsp;
in all, everyone in attendance had a damn good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:12.960
time that night. They’d spend the rest of the&nbsp;
early morning setting rocks on fire for fun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:18.480
and chewing on ignited fireworks. That’s the&nbsp;
kind of brain trust we’re dealing with here.

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:21.280
When the Foundation eventually&nbsp;
contained them in Vulture Gulch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:25.280
the gearheads didn’t even put up a fuss,&nbsp;
as long the Foundation kept supplying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:30.240
them with three decommissioned vehicles&nbsp;
every month. It’s a pretty sweet deal:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:36.560
A crazed car-lover’s paradise, where as long as&nbsp;
you keep it within the walls, anything goes, baby.

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:42.800
But there is one strange little detail. A&nbsp;
question that remains unanswered. Drones sent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:47.040
in by the Foundation to spy on the residents&nbsp;
of Vulture Gulch have picked up one strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:53.360
recurring theme in their chatter: Mentions of an&nbsp;
individual known only as “The Boss” paying them a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:59.360
visit. And we can only assume they don’t mean&nbsp;
Bruce Springsteen. The only clues we have are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:05.280
that the Gearheads believe this Boss created them&nbsp;
and put them here on this earth to be totally rad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:12.320
The other clue is a seemingly pervasive belief&nbsp;
that, someday soon, the Boss will return.

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:15.520
Who do you think the boss of the&nbsp;
Exploding Zombie Gearheads truly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:18.080
is? Let us know down in the comments.

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:22.880
Now go check out “Top 15 Most Dangerous&nbsp;
SCP Monsters in Containment” and “Evil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:28.080
Monster Created by SCP Foundation&nbsp;
SCP-2419 - The Laughing Men”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.760
for more of the biggest bad&nbsp;
boys in Foundation history!

